    <p>The Grownsy takes roughly twice as long to reset, and the extra time is not rinsing — it is caution. Its warning card adds steps the NoseFrida never has: turn the device off right after suction to avoid mucus backflow, keep liquid out of the machine, and keep the chamber dry. Those steps are manageable in daylight and annoying at 3AM. For the electric side of the tradeoff in detail, see our <a href="/tests/nosefrida-vs-grownsy-at-3am/">NoseFrida vs Grownsy pilot test</a>.</p>
    <p>The other two models on our shortlist — the Momcozy BreezyClear and the Braun BNA100US — have not been through the timed test, so we have no cleaning times for them. Everything about their cleanup is manufacturer spec, not our measurement, and we do not rank what we have not measured.</p>
